! mcp_bootstrap_p114.strap -- "MCP FURNISHED PTOE", printed page 114.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.121, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID
! DC000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 114".
!
! FORTY-EIGHT LINES, COUNTED NOT ESTIMATED.  The printed LINE column
! runs 1..48 with no gap and the form is blank below line 48.  The
! card-serial column runs DC000001 (line 1) through DC000048 (line
! 48) -- ONE CARD PER LINE, forty-eight cards, with no serial
! repeated (unlike printed p.112, where a SIC and its branch share a
! card).  A NEW PUNCHED DECK STARTS HERE: the serial restarts at
! 000001 with the prefix "DC", where printed p.112 was punching
! DB0000nn.  The header's own CARD ID repeats line 1's serial.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS, FROM A PRIMARY SOURCE THAT DESCRIBES IT EXACTLY
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! docs/ocr/C22-6728-1_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt, "The Program
! Table of Exits (PTOE)" and "The MCP PTOE and the Standard Fixup"
! (PDF pp.14-15), is this page in prose:
!
!   "The MCP PTOE is located at SFPTE.  It has the same structure as
!    the PP PTOE, and contains ones in the pattern word corresponding
!    to each of the maskable interrupts.  The last 27 full word entry
!    points are all of the form
!         LVI, $1, YIN**
!         B,   YMSF
!    (** denotes the location of the indicator mnemonic)
!    NOTE: The first two interrupts, TS and EXE, are treated as
!    masked off, and the PTOE branches to the return after maskable
!    routine (WRAM)."
!
! and the PTOE's layout is given as "4+k full words":
!    word 1  saved IC        word 2  saved $IND
!    word 3  saved $MASK     word 4  pattern word, containing k ones
!    word 4+i  first instruction for the ith special interrupt
!              routine, i counted through the ONE bits of the
!              pattern word in indicator order.
!
! This page is exactly that:
!   line  5  S FPTE DRZ(N),(3)   -- words 1-3, the IC/$IND/$MASK save
!                                   area, 215163.00..215165.77.
!   line  6  DD(BU,64),(8)...    -- word 4, THE PATTERN WORD, at
!                                   215166.00.
!   lines 7-10  words 4+1 and 4+2: the TS and EXE entries, which do
!               NOT use the standard fixup -- "B,YFXTS / NOP" and
!               "B,YEXEFX / NOP", and printed p.133 defines both
!               YFXTS (216530.00) and YEXEFX (216530.40) as "B,WRAM",
!               the return-after-maskable routine the guide names.
!   lines 11-48  nineteen of the twenty-seven "LVI,$1,YIN** / B,YMSF"
!               entries.
!
! >>> WHAT THIS PREDICTS FOR printed p.115, AS A CROSS-PAGE CHECK. <<<
! The guide fixes the count at twenty-seven.  This page spends
! nineteen (DF..BTR), so printed p.115 must carry EXACTLY EIGHT more
! -- DTR and PG0..PG6, in that order -- and then the table ends.
! MEASURED, not inferred: the OCR of PDF p.122 (printed p.115) opens
!   line 1  215214.00  216577.03 01  LVI,$1,YINDTR
!   line 2  215214.40  216531.10 00  B,YMSF
!   line 3  215215.00  216577.43 01  LVI,$1,YINPG0
!   ...
!   line 7  215217.00  216600.43 01  LVI,$1,YINPG2
! so it resumes at 215214.00, contiguous with this page's last row
! at 215213.40, and sixteen half words later the PTOE is complete at
! 215223.40.  A p.115 reading that does not land there is wrong, or
! this one is.
!
! >>> THE PATTERN WORD IS VERIFIED AGAINST THE GUIDE, BIT BY BIT. <<<
! The guide says "Only bits 4, 18, 20, and 22 through 47 may be set
! to one in the pattern word.  All others are treated as zero."
! Line 6's twenty-two printed octal digits
!     0 0 4 0 0 0 1 2 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 6 0 0 0 0 0
! decode, as bit 0 then twenty-one groups of three, to exactly
!     bit 4, bit 18, bit 20, bits 22-47 and nothing else
! -- 29 ones.  Twenty-nine entries, of which the first two (bit 4 =
! TS, bit 18 = EXE) are lines 7-10, leaves TWENTY-SEVEN "LVI,$1,YIN**"
! entries, which is the number the guide states.  Bit 21 (IF) is off,
! as the guide requires.  This is an independent check of the whole
! word from a typeset source, not a re-reading of the drum print.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN, AND HOW THE COUNTER GETS HERE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the origin, and this
! page is OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G block that printed p.2 opened and
! printed p.98 line 37 closed, so names here may repeat names from
! pp.2-98 at different addresses.  None here does.
!
! Line 4 prints "215163.00 *" against the statement "SLC,$" -- an
! SLC to the counter's own current value, which moves nothing.  The
! counter arrives at 215163.00 on its own: printed p.112 ends at
! 215146.40 and printed p.113 (PDF p.120) runs 215147.00..215162.40,
! its last row a half word "B,W LODE" at 215162.40, so the next free
! half word IS 215163.00.  CONTIGUOUS, measured in the OCR of PDF
! p.120 and not inferred.  This deck therefore sets the origin with
! an explicit "SLC,(8)215163.0" and then carries the printed
! "SLC,$" as line 4, which assembles and changes nothing.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE NINETEEN YIN** NAMES ARE SETTLED BY A TABLE, NOT BY INK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every operand on lines 11-47 is "YIN" + a 7030 INDICATOR MNEMONIC,
! and strap/opcodes.py's INDICATOR_BITS (from the Reference Manual's
! Figure 11) gives the mnemonics and their bit numbers:
!   DF 20, IF 21, LC 22, PF 23, ZD 24, IR 25, LS 26, PSH 27,
!   XPFP 28, XPO 29, XPH 30, XPL 31, XPU 32, ZM 33, RU 34, TF 35,
!   UF 36, VF 37, XF 38, BTR 39, DTR 40, PG0..PG6 41-47.
! This page's operands, in printed order, are
!   DF LC PF ZD IR LS PSH XPF XPO XPH XPL XPU ZM RU TF UF VF XF BTR
! -- bits 20, 22, 23, 24, ... 39 with IF (21) skipped, which is the
! pattern word's one-bits in order.  So LC really is a C (Lost
! Carry), ZD really is a D (Zero Divisor) and XPO really is an O
! (eXPonent Overflow); none of the three rests on the drum.
!
! CORROBORATED A SECOND TIME, by the Y table's OWN DEFINING CARDS.
! docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt, PDF p.141 (printed p.134), prints
! one card per indicator in the form "YIN** (AA)DD(BU,32),**" -- the
! mnemonic again, as a four-character datum -- at
!   216566.00 YINDF   216566.40 YINLC   216567.00 YINPF
!   216567.40 YINZD   216570.00 YINIR   216570.40 YINLS
!   216571.00 YINPSH  216571.40 YINXPF  216572.00 YINXPO
!   216572.40 YINXPH  216573.00 YINXPL  216573.40 YINZM
!   216574.00 YINRU   216574.40 YINTF   216575.00 YINUF
!   216575.40 YINVF   216576.00 YINXF   216576.40 YINBTR
!   216577.00 YINDTR  216577.40 YINPG0  ...  216602.40 YINPG6
!   216603.00 YINXPU
! which is where every SYN below comes from.  It also EXPLAINS THE
! PAGE'S ONE ANOMALY: line 33's operand is 216603.03 where its
! neighbours are 216573.03 and 216573.43.  YINXPU is not in the
! table's main run at all -- it was appended AFTER the seven program
! indicators -- so the page's entry for it, which must appear in
! pattern-word order between XPL and ZM, points thirty words away.
! Read, cross-checked, and not an error.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE LVI IMMEDIATE PINS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "LVI,$1,SYM" puts bits 0-18 of SYM's BIT address in the value
! field (strap_asm: eval_addr_field shift 5), so the printed half
! word is (bitaddr & ~31) | 3 -- the symbol's HALF WORD, and nothing
! finer.  216566.03 means "somewhere in 216566.00..216566.37" and
! 216566.43 means "somewhere in 216566.40..216566.77".  The .00/.40
! values written below are therefore NOT this page's reading; they
! come from the defining cards on printed p.134 listed above.  The
! trailing "3" in ".03"/".43" is the J field for $1 and is the same
! on every one of the nineteen rows; printed pp.89-95 print ".03"
! for the identically-indexed "LVI,TMX1,...".
!
! The three branch targets are pinned the same way and corroborated
! the same way: "B,YFXTS" prints 216530.10 and printed p.133 line 18
! defines "YFXTS B,WRAM" at 216530.00; "B,YEXEFX" prints 216530.50
! and p.133 line 19 defines YEXEFX at 216530.40; "B,YMSF" prints
! 216531.10 and p.133 line 20 defines "YMSF TI1,16,STLR,SLRBU" at
! 216531.00.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE TWO NAMES THIS PAGE DEFINES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! S FPTE (line 5) is printed "SFPTE" with no embedded blank, read at
! 1200 dpi, and it is referenced twice elsewhere in the listing at
! THIS address: PDF p.137 prints "WCCNA LVI,$1,SFPTE" compiling
! 215163.03, and PDF p.151 prints "WRAWM LVI,$1,SFPTE" compiling
! 215163.03.  The guide's sentence "The MCP PTOE is located at
! SFPTE" is a third, typeset witness to the spelling.
!
! ST FIX (line 7) is printed with an embedded blank and becomes
! STFIX once blanks are dropped, as on every page since p.2.  IT IS
! REFERENCED NOWHERE ELSE IN THE LISTING -- grepping the full-volume
! OCR for "ST FIX" returns only this page's own line 7 -- so unlike
! SFPTE it rests on ink alone.  The risk is small because S, T, F, I
! and X carry none of this drum's round-glyph or B/8 hazards, but it
! is recorded rather than left implied.
!
! The word 4 pattern itself carries no name on this page.  It has
! one elsewhere: PDF p.137 prints "WPATT SYN,SFPTE+3.0" resolving to
! 215166.00, which is line 6's location.  Not needed here, not
! declared here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This page opens round glyphs as every page in this volume does --
! its own column heading prints "LCCATICN" for LOCATION, and nearly
! every ".00" in the LOCATION and BINARY columns prints ".CC".  All
! of those are octal fields and are read as 0 with certainty.
!
! The twenty-two digits of line 6 were NOT read by eye.  The glyphs
! were sliced on the print's own 1/10-inch pitch at 1200 dpi and
! clustered by shape; nine clusters came back and resolve to
! 0, 4, 1, 2, 7, 7(variant), 6, 0, 0 -- six distinct digits.  The
! same procedure on the STATEMENT column's copy of the constant
! returns the identical twenty digits.  Counting them by eye had
! given four zeros between the 4 and the 1 where there are three.
!
! The remaining round glyphs are all inside YIN** names and are
! settled by the indicator table above, not by shape.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TWO LISTING MARKS, RECORDED AND NOT EXPLAINED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 4 prints a bare "*" after its location ("215163.00 *") and so
! does line 27 ("215201.00 *").  printed pp.103, 110 and 112 carry
! the same mark.  Neither changes a compiled bit and neither is
! checked here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) Blanks inside symbol names are dropped: S FPTE -> SFPTE,
!     ST FIX -> STFIX.
! (2) Line 31 prints "LVI,$1 ,YINXPL" with a space before the comma,
!     which is the card's own column spacing and not a datum; it is
!     written "LVI, $1, YINXPL" here.
! (3) Nothing else.  No printed spelling was rejected by strap_asm;
!     "SLC,$" and "DRZ(N),(3)" both assemble as printed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHICH ROWS ARE INDEPENDENT CHECKS, AND WHICH ARE NOT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The forty-two instruction rows all name externals, so their
! ADDRESS halves came from the same print they are checked against
! and only the opcode/modifier bits and the LOCATION are an
! independent check.  What IS independent on this page:
!   * every LOCATION, against a counter started at 215163.00 and
!     advanced by the page's own statements -- and the start itself
!     is fixed by printed p.113's last row, not by this page;
!   * line 6's whole 64-bit pattern word, against the guide's
!     "bits 4, 18, 20, and 22 through 47";
!   * SFPTE's address, against two LVI immediates on pp.130 and 144;
!   * the nineteen YIN** addresses, against the defining cards on
!     printed p.134 -- a different page of the same listing.
! Line 5's DRZ gets no !CHECK: "000003.00" is the RESERVATION COUNT
! printed in the BINARY OUTPUT column, not storage contents, and
! nothing is deposited for the oracle to read.  printed pp.84 and
! 109 give their DRZ rows no !CHECK for the same reason.
! Line 4 gets none either -- an SLC prints no binary.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

        SLC, (8)215163.0

! Externals.  Addresses from printed p.133 (YFXTS, YEXEFX, YMSF) and
! printed p.134 (every YIN**), both via the full-volume OCR.
YFXTS   SYN, (8)216530.0             ! p.133 "YFXTS  B,WRAM"
YEXEFX  SYN, (8)216530.40            ! p.133 "YEXEFX B,WRAM"
YMSF    SYN, (8)216531.0             ! p.133 "YMSF   TI1,16,STLR,SLRBU"
YINDF   SYN, (8)216566.0             ! p.134 "YINDF   (AA)DD(BU,32),DF"
YINLC   SYN, (8)216566.40            ! p.134 "YINLC   (AA)DD(BU,32),LC"
YINPF   SYN, (8)216567.0             ! p.134 "YINPF   (AA)DD(BU,32),PF"
YINZD   SYN, (8)216567.40            ! p.134 "YINZD   (AA)DD(BU,32),ZD"
YINIR   SYN, (8)216570.0             ! p.134 "YINIR   (AA)DD(BU,32),IR"
YINLS   SYN, (8)216570.40            ! p.134 "YINLS   (AA)DD(BU,32),LS"
YINPSH  SYN, (8)216571.0             ! p.134 "YINPSH  (AA)DD(BU,32),PSH"
YINXPF  SYN, (8)216571.40            ! p.134 "YINXPF  (AA)DD(BU,32),XPFP"
YINXPO  SYN, (8)216572.0             ! p.134 "YINXPO  (AA)DD(BU,32),XPO"
YINXPH  SYN, (8)216572.40            ! p.134 "YINXPH  (AA)DD(BU,32),XPH"
YINXPL  SYN, (8)216573.0             ! p.134 "YINXPL  (AA)DD(BU,32),XPL"
YINXPU  SYN, (8)216603.0             ! p.134, APPENDED AFTER YINPG6
YINZM   SYN, (8)216573.40            ! p.134 "YINZM   (AA)DD(BU,32),ZM"
YINRU   SYN, (8)216574.0             ! p.134 "YINRU   (AA)DD(BU,32),RU"
YINTF   SYN, (8)216574.40            ! p.134 "YINTF   (AA)DD(BU,32),TF"
YINUF   SYN, (8)216575.0             ! p.134 "YINUF   (AA)DD(BU,32),UF"
YINVF   SYN, (8)216575.40            ! p.134 "YINVF   (AA)DD(BU,32),VF"
YINXF   SYN, (8)216576.0             ! p.134 "YINXF   (AA)DD(BU,32),XF"
YINBTR  SYN, (8)216576.40            ! p.134 "YINBTR  (AA)DD(BU,32),BTR"

        SLC, (8)215163.0
        SLC, $                       ! line  4, as printed

SFPTE   DRZ(N), (3)                  ! line  5 -MCP TOE
        DD(BU,64), (8)40001277777777600000    ! line 6 -PATTERN
STFIX   B, YFXTS                     ! line  7
        NOP                          ! line  8
        B, YEXEFX                    ! line  9
        NOP                          ! line 10
        LVI, $1, YINDF               ! line 11
        B, YMSF                      ! line 12
